  "problem": "PHC4, APCD, facility licensure and closure tracking could lack explicit state scope. One state's coverage could imply all-state completeness. Publisher authority could be inferred from a familiar title. Scraping a public page could bypass an application or DUA. Pennsylvania finance could claim identical PHC4/HCRIS reporting definitions or unrestricted payload access. A small state pilot could be converted into a national completeness claim. Nongovernmental Sheps Center operator identity could be replaced by CMS enrollment files.",
  "resulting_behavior": "State intake lives in packages/connectors/source-registry/state-intake.mjs with four frozen family records. One state's coverage never implies all-state completeness. Publisher authority is not inferred from a familiar title. Known portal/API boundaries have fixtures and budgets; scraping does not bypass an application or DUA. The Pennsylvania finance task returns PHC4 alongside HCRIS without identical reporting definitions or unrestricted payload access. No national completeness claim is derived from a small state pilot. Sheps Center operator identity is preserved. Frozen named-source-registry.v1.0.0.json, connector src, retrieval ranking and coverage accounting artifacts are unchanged. Last-good generation live-2026-09-03-85b50522b420 is unchanged.",
